NOTICE
======

This repository contains code, configuration and result files for a course
project on canteen food recognition.  It does NOT redistribute any of the
image datasets listed below; every dataset stays where its authors publish it,
and the paths in the README refer to a local copy produced by the download
scripts.  If you reproduce this work, download the data yourself and accept
each licence on its own terms.

1. Food-101
   Authors: Lukas Bossard, Matthieu Guillaumin, Luc Van Gool (ETH Zurich).
   Project page: https://data.vision.ee.ethz.ch/cvl/datasets_extra/food-101/
   Mirror used here: https://huggingface.co/datasets/ethz/food101
   Licence: the dataset is distributed for research use; images are collected
   from the web and remain the property of their original owners.  Food-101 is
   used here for coursework and research only.

2. Food-101N (noisy Food-101 with CleanNet verification labels)
   Authors: Kuang-Huei Lee et al. (CleanNet, arXiv:1711.07131).
   Project page: https://kuanghuei.github.io/Food-101N/
   Download: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kuanghueilee/food-101n
   Licence: released by the authors for research use under the terms stated on
   the project page / Kaggle dataset card.  This project used a 20-class subset
   (69,512 images) for the E7 fine-tuning experiment (README section 5.8).

3. 16 famous Chinese dishes
   Source: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/patzer0/16-famous-chinese-dishes
   Licence: as stated on the Kaggle dataset card; images remain the property of
   their original owners.  Used to extend the 20-class model to 116 classes
   (README section 5.5); Peking duck was merged into Food-101's peking_duck.

4. CNFOOD-241
   Authors: the CNFOOD-241 dataset, published on Mendeley Data,
   https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fspyss5zbb (DOI 10.17632/fspyss5zbb,
   contributed by Shenzhen Institutes of Advanced Technology, CAS)
   Method paper: PLOS ONE, doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0358248 (the Mendeley page
   lists the full citation).
   Licence: CC BY-NC 3.0 (Attribution-NonCommercial 3.0 Unported,
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0).  The dataset card states:
   "As some of the images in the dataset are from ChineseFoodNet, they are not
   supported for commercial use."  ChineseFoodNet itself
   (https://sites.google.com/view/chinesefoodnet/) is likewise restricted to
   non-commercial research.  This project used 20 of its
   241 classes (21,043 images) for the canteen head described in README
   section 5.7, strictly for coursework; no images are redistributed here and
   the trained checkpoint must not be used commercially either.

5. Chain nutrition reference
   The per-serving calorie figures shown in the web demo come from the official
   McDonald's China nutrition calculator, scraped into
   data/external/brand_menu.json by scripts/fetch_brand_nutrition.py.  They are
   quoted as reference values only, with attribution, and are not part of any
   model training.

